---
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Amazon from '../components/Amazon.astro';
import ArtImage from '../components/ArtImage.astro';
import { path } from '../site';
const books=(await getCollection('books',({data})=>data.published)).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
const book=books[0];const {Content}=await render(book);
const bookUrl=new URL(path('story/'),Astro.site).href;
const bookSchema={
  '@context':'https://schema.org',
  '@graph':[
    {'@type':'Book','@id':`${bookUrl}#book`,name:`${book.data.title}: ${book.data.subtitle}`,author:{'@type':'Person',name:book.data.author},description:book.data.description,url:bookUrl,sameAs:book.data.amazon,inLanguage:'en',genre:'Dark fantasy',image:new URL(path('cover-art.webp'),Astro.site).href,...(book.data.paperback ? {isbn:book.data.paperback.isbn,numberOfPages:book.data.paperback.pages,bookFormat:'https://schema.org/Paperback'} : {})},
    {'@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:new URL(path(),Astro.site).href},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'The book',item:bookUrl}]}
  ]
};
---
<Layout title="The Book: A Cradle Made of Embers" description={book.data.description} schema={bookSchema}>
  <section class="page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">ILLUSTRATED DARK FANTASY / YH</p>
    <h1>A Monster’s <em>Mother</em></h1>
    <p>A Cradle Made of Embers · A dragon fantasy novel about motherhood and survival</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose story-prose">
    <Content/>
    {book.data.paperback && <section class="edition-details" aria-labelledby="paperback-details">
      <h2 id="paperback-details">Paperback edition details</h2>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Author</dt><dd>{book.data.author}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Format</dt><dd>Paperback · black-and-white interior illustrations</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Print length</dt><dd>{book.data.paperback.pages} pages</dd></div>
        <div><dt>ISBN-13</dt><dd>{book.data.paperback.isbn}</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>These details identify the English paperback. Check the <a href={book.data.amazon} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Amazon listing</a> for the current price and delivery to your country.</p>
    </section>}
    <div class="actions"><Amazon/><a class="text-link" href={path('read/')}>Read Chapter One free →</a></div>
    <section aria-labelledby="before-reading">
      <h2 id="before-reading">Before you begin reading</h2>
      <h3>What is A Monster’s Mother about?</h3>
      <p>Elara gives birth to Ember, a child with scales and wings. Taking him home is only the beginning: she must care for a growing dragon while hiding him from neighbours who may see him as a threat. The story follows the bond between mother and son, rather than a dragon rider’s quest for power.</p>
      <p>The opening chapter starts in a snowbound cave. You can <a href={path('read/')}>read “The First Breath” free</a> to experience the writing before deciding whether the book is for you. No account or email address is required to read it.</p>
      <h3>Is this the complete book for free?</h3>
      <p>No. This website shares the first chapter, not the full novel. The Amazon link above takes you to the book’s listing, where you can check the available edition, current price and delivery options for your country.</p>
      <h3>What language is the novel in?</h3>
      <p>The novel and the free chapter are in English. The French, Arabic and Turkish versions of this website introduce the story and its world; they are not translated editions of the novel.</p>
      <h3>Does the book include illustrations?</h3>
      <p>Yes. It is an illustrated dark fantasy novel. Its black-and-white interior drawings accompany the story; the colour artwork on this website introduces the characters and atmosphere. You can meet <a href={path('characters/elara/')}>Elara</a> and <a href={path('characters/ember/')}>Ember</a> before reading.</p>
      <figure class="paperback-preview" id="paperback-preview">
        <ArtImage src={path('interior-page-8.webp')} alt="Black-and-white interior page showing Elara holding the newborn dragon beside a snowy cave, with printed page number 8." loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 600px) 90vw, 420px"/>
        <figcaption>Inside the illustrated paperback: page 8, from Chapter Two, “Back Through the Snow”.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>This is a digital preview of a page from the English 6 × 9-inch paperback, including its margins and page number. It shows the interior drawing style, not the colour artwork used to present the book on this site. Contrast on printed paper can differ from a screen.</p>
      <h3>Is The Mothers Monster the same title?</h3>
      <p><i>The Mothers Monster</i>, also presented as <i>She Gave Birth to a Dragon</i>, is the video title. <i>A Monster’s Mother: A Cradle Made of Embers</i> is the novel by YH featured here. Visit the <a href={path('movie/')}>film page</a> for the video and its source, or begin with the book’s free chapter.</p>
      <h3>Who might enjoy this dragon fantasy?</h3>
      <p>Readers drawn to protective mothers, misunderstood creatures and difficult choices may find a way into Elara and Ember’s story. The central relationship is maternal, not a promised romantic pairing. The free chapter is the simplest way to judge the tone and decide whether to continue.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href={path('read/')}>Begin Chapter One →</a><Amazon/></div>
  </section>
  {books.length>1 && <section class="section"><h2>Continue the series</h2>{books.slice(1).map(b=><article><h3>{b.data.title}: {b.data.subtitle}</h3><p>{b.data.description}</p>{b.data.amazon && <a href={b.data.amazon}>Find the book on Amazon</a>}</article>)}</section>}
</Layout>

<style>
  .edition-details{border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding-block:1.5rem;margin-block:2rem}
  .edition-details dl{margin:1rem 0}
  .edition-details dl div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(6rem,1fr) 2fr;gap:1rem;padding-block:.35rem}
  .edition-details dt{font-weight:600}
  .edition-details dd{margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
  @media(max-width:400px){.edition-details dl div{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.1rem}}
  .paperback-preview{max-width:420px;margin:2rem auto}
  .paperback-preview :global(img){display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:#fff}
  .paperback-preview figcaption{font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);margin-top:1rem}
</style>
